On May 7, 10:26 pm, "3cnf...@gmail.com" <3cnf...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I need help accomplishing a speed run. My character, a dwarvish
> archaeologist, just completed a protection run with all 9 units of
> protection... and then found a *wand of wishing (0:3)*. What's more,
> he got GDSM from a bones pile. WOW.

Very impressive work in making the run, and good luck with the wand
and bones!!!
First, a caveat: I don't know what "speed run" means in your case.  My
fastest is sub 18k but I wouldn't have made it if not for finding some
bones piles at about turn 12k.  I'll give you a few comments though
that helped me.

>
> It's turn 6400 or so. My relevant equipment is:
> 1. armor: AC-13. Have clock of displacement and GDSM. There's a +2
> dwarvish mithril coat in the mines if I want both displacement and
> MC3.

nono, stay with the MR from the scales.  No doubt in my mind.

> 2. uncursed luckstone

bless it to give yourself +3 luck.  When you see a coaligned altar
throw a #named or id'ed gem at it but don't chase it around the level
trying to max out.  When you see an altar do a couple of sacs but
don't spend a lot of time at it.  Luck is good but as long as it is
sufficiently positive you'll be okay.

> 3. oilskin sack, 1000 gold and a ruby for buying from shops.

For a speed run you'll need a blessed greased bag of holding.  Forget
about re-stashing your loot.  Just leave your exit gear, like GD
scrolls and confuson/booze/tripe in the main dungeon at the top of the
mines for picking up before you go to the Planes.

> 4. a ID'd, uncursed scroll of charging, but not !ea or !ew. Well, that
> takes care of the "2 blessed scrolls of charging" wish. :)

Fantastic, that saves you a wish!  Use it for a magic marker and don't
forget to write 2 scrolls (one for the wand and one for the magic
marker)  Don't worry about not having ?oEW.  With jumping boots, self-
teleport, and Elbereth-ing you can pick your battles.

> 5. a crystall ball and tooled horn, left at Minetown to avoid
> burdening myself.

keep the horn so that you don't have to waste time fighting and leave
the crystal ball in your exit-gear.  Keep in mind that you'll also
have your quest artifact for portal detection.

> 7. Most underwhelmingly, wielding a rusty dwarvish mattock. I only
> know the protection spell, so maybe I shouldn't focus on casting
> spells. Oh, and about 6 unidentified wands that could be price ID'd at
> the general store where I just found the wand.

You've got a heavy weapon but I suppose you can save time with it by
digging.  Because I can be lazy, I will sometimes #twoweapon a silver
saber and a pick-axe.  It's fun to be a cuisinart but not necessary.
Don't leave too many of the stair locations unknown in the main
dungeon and possibly none of Gehennom's stairs unknown; spend a few
extra turns knowing your escape route.  Keep in mind that magic
mapping scrolls are fairly inexpensive to write.

To save time, just engrave id the wands; don't worry about the wasted
charge.  If you don't get a message drop your lizard corpse and your
bag in front of a door and that'll tell you a bunch.

>
> What techniques would you suggest for such a speed run, and what would
> you wish for? Should I wish up most of an ascension kit and dig for
> the castle's wand of wishing? Should I wish for a magic marker, write
> a bunch of scrolls of earth (cheapest scroll to write) for minotaur
> defense, and use those and the tooled horn to play defensively until
> the castle like some other speed ascender did? Should I wish for
> Gauntlets of Power so I'm not a wimpy, burdened little breadstick for
> the next monster (strength is 11 or so, and already burdened again
> from picking up *scrolls*)? Speed boots or jumping boots? AAGH brain
> spinning...

The basic technique is to not wait for the RNG to gift you what you
need, just wish for it.  In my experience, the game starts speeding up
once I find my precious ring of teleport control.  Once I have that I
eat leprechauns and I'm warping my way through the dungeon.  And once
I have a source of MR then it's full speed ahead!  If you really want
to save time then don't complete Sokoban, just get the earth scrolls,
wand, ring, and food from the first level.

Don't worry about minotaurs, save your sleep zaps for them if you
covet their wands of digging but otherwise just leave them in the
dust.  Your AC is not the greatest but should be okay once you start
adding some wardrobe.  blessed fixed +3 jumping boots will give you an
additional -4 ac!  Having jumping boots also serves as a not so gentle
reminder to stay un-burdened.

Str=11 is unfortunate, but gauntlets of power is not the greatest
wish, IMO.  Possibly better IMO to bless your tinning kit and tin the
giants that you find.  Once you have STR=18/** and complete (enough)
intrinsics you can dump the tinning kit.  A blessed bag of holding
will help somewhat, as will leveling up and finding more giants.
Fortunately they come in packs so you can make 3 or 4 tins with each
encounter.  OTOH, if you have wishes to spare, and don't plan on
needing a whole lot of spells, and can't get out of the Mines
unburdened, then yes, wish for them.

By the way, are you sure that you did not lose strength from
poisoning?  have you applied a unicorn horn?

Jumping boots are my speed ascension footwear of choice.  I bring
along a pair of speed boots for levitating through the planes, though,
but that risks losing any rings, such as levitation.  When jumping
food can be a big problem, though, and especially if you are
^Teleporting your way through the dungeon.  In a 20-30k speed
ascension with teleports and boots I've gone through almost all of the
rations (food, K, C, and cram) in the dungeon.

Good luck and good skill !  Also, don't be afraid to slow down.  A
good recuperation break of 1000 turns won't appear so bad compared to
the total turns, but it's a shame to suffer YASD when all is going so
well.  It's possible to get to the very end and not have enough kit to
accomplish a task.  Be somewhat frugal with your wand of wishing zaps
and use them for emergencies.  Don't use them all up on weapons or
even armor, you might need a cockatrice corpse or a helm of opposite
alignment on the Astral Plane.

